body:
Can we add a temporary "fix" to make IDEs happy? like this (`HttpKernel/Client`):

``` php
<?php
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;

    /**
     * @return Response
     */
    public function getResponse()
    {
        return parent::getResponse();
    }
```

@biozshock both responses are different.

The proper fix would be #4497 but it has been rejected because it is a BC break. Unfortunately, we cannot fix this issue without a BC break, either for the HttpKernel client or for all other BrowserKit users (by changing the API of the BrowserKit response).

Making BrowserKit depend on HttpFoundation does not make sense through. `HttpFoundation\Response` represents a response you are sending, whether BrowserKit represents the client side
